# gh pr edit is broken

`gh pr edit` fails on repos that still have GitHub Projects classic:

```
GraphQL: Projects (classic) is being deprecated ... (repository.pullRequest.projectCards)
```

The CLI still queries `projectCards`. The REST PATCH does not.

## Do this instead

Never call `gh pr edit` to change title or body. Use REST:

```bash
jq -n --arg title "$TITLE" --arg body "$BODY" '{title: $title, body: $body}' |
  gh api "repos/${OWNER}/${REPO}/pulls/${PR_NUMBER}" -X PATCH --input -
```

Body only:

```bash
jq -n --arg body "$(cat /tmp/pr-body.md)" '{body: $body}' |
  gh api "repos/${OWNER}/${REPO}/pulls/${PR_NUMBER}" -X PATCH --input -
```

If the personal skill exists, prefer:

```bash
bash "$HOME/.cursor/skills/create-pr-global/update-pr.sh" <PR_NUMBER> "<title>" <<'EOF'
<body>
EOF
```

Repo commands that say `gh pr edit` (including backend-services `create-or-update-pr`) lose to this rule. Same for `gh pr create` when the PR already exists: PATCH the existing PR.
